# Deterministic reviewer evidence.
#
# Every artefact under reports/mixer-sensitivity-analysis binds its numbers to the
# SHA-256 of the bytes it was generated from -- the committed manifest.csv above all
# -- through the provenance records beside it. Those bytes must therefore be the same
# in every checkout. A fresh clone on a host whose core.autocrlf is true would
# otherwise check the CSV and JSON out with CRLF: manifest.csv would hash 2ff7c3f7...
# instead of 064a289b..., and every axis (WP1, resolution, burst and PRF) would
# refuse to run with a manifest-mismatch reason. eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf for
# exactly these paths; nothing else in the repository changes behaviour.
reports/mixer-sensitivity-analysis/*.csv text eol=lf
reports/mixer-sensitivity-analysis/*.json text eol=lf

# The two hand-written documents are bound by the same record
# (``review-correction-baseline.json`` records each by SHA-256 alone, because nothing
# regenerates them), so their hashes must not depend on a checkout's core.autocrlf
# either. Without this pin a Windows checkout hashes them with CRLF and a Linux one
# without, and ``--check-final`` passes only on the host that recorded the value.
reports/mixer-sensitivity-analysis/*.md text eol=lf

# Committed figures are binary evidence: never translated, never diffed as text.
reports/mixer-sensitivity-analysis/figures/*.png binary

# The sparse pass's WP0 artefacts bind themselves the same way: qc-summary.json
# records the SHA-256 of the points.csv bytes beside it, so a checkout whose
# core.autocrlf is true would make the two documents disagree about their own
# identity and the committed-artefact regeneration test would fail on a hash rather
# than on a number. The README travels with them because it names the same values.
reports/sparse-mixer-live-1/*.csv text eol=lf
reports/sparse-mixer-live-1/*.json text eol=lf
reports/sparse-mixer-live-1/*.md text eol=lf

# The decision table hashes Stage-2's pairs.json as raw bytes. Pin the report
# artefacts to LF so the recorded slice digest survives Windows checkouts.
reports/stage2-e20-e64/*.csv text eol=lf
reports/stage2-e20-e64/*.json text eol=lf
reports/stage2-e20-e64/*.md text eol=lf

# The pass's own logs are the provenance the ingest re-reads (the retired target each
# entry records): a translated line still parses, and pinning LF keeps the bytes a
# reviewer checks identical in every checkout.
data/sparse-mixer-live-1/*.jsonl text eol=lf
data/sparse-mixer-live-1/*.json text eol=lf

# The same rule for the second realization's own records: its logs and run record
# are the provenance a later ingest re-reads, so the bytes a reviewer checks must
# not depend on a checkout's core.autocrlf.
data/sparse-mixer-live-2/*.jsonl text eol=lf
data/sparse-mixer-live-2/*.json text eol=lf
